  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>randg</keyword>
  <short_description>Gamma distributed random number.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>M = randg</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>M = randg(A)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>M = randg(A, n)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>M = randg(A, x1, x2, ... , xN)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>M = randg(A, sz)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>M = randg(A, x1, x2, ... , xN, classname)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>A</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a real nonnegative value or array: the shape parameter(s).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>n</param_name>
      <param_description
      >a variable: n-by-n matrix will be generated.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>x1, x2, ... , xN</param_name>
      <param_description>x1-by-...-by-xN values</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>classname</param_name>
      <param_description>a string: &apos;single&apos; or &apos;double&apos;
      </param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>M</param_name>
      <param_description>a matrix of random numbers.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>
      <b>randg</b> returns a matrix with gamma distributed random elements, with shape parameter <b
      >A</b> and unit scale.</p>
    <p>A gamma sample of shape <b>k</b> has mean <b>k</b> and variance <b>k</b>; a shape of 1 gives the standard exponential distribution.</p>
    <p>When only <b>A</b> is supplied, the result has the size of <b
      >A</b> and each element uses the matching shape. When a size is supplied, <b
      >A</b> must be a scalar used for every element.</p>
    <p>Values are drawn with the Marsaglia and Tsang rejection method; the seed can be modified using <b
      >rng</b>.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography>G. Marsaglia and W. W. Tsang, "A simple method for generating gamma variables", ACM Transactions on Mathematical Software, 26(3), 363-372, 2000.</bibliography>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[rng('default');
randg
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[rng('default');
randg(2, 3)
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[rng('default');
M = randg(3, 1, 100000);
[mean(M), var(M)]
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data
        runnable="cli"
      ><![CDATA[rng('default');
randg(2, 2, 2, 'single')
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
